1.	Description of Services and Deliverables.

1.A    SERVICES.
Axiom Consulting will work with You to implement the Axiom Fusion Applications for below scoped entities. Axiom Consulting will implement the standard functionality described in section 1.A.4 Module Functional Scope and associated Appendices, using the Axiom True Cloud Methodology (ACTM).

1.A.1 Definitions
Within this exhibit, the following definitions will apply:
•	You and Your shall mean SmartAir Airlines ("You", "the Customer", "SkyServe", "SmartAir Airlines", "SA").
•	Axiom Cloud Services shall mean the Axiom Software as a Service ("SaaS") offerings and related Axiom Programs subscribed by the Customer.
•	Standard functionality shall mean the standard functionality of the Axiom Programs as set out in the relevant Program Documentation.
•	Axiom Modern Best Practice(s) shall mean a collection of business processes pre-defined by Axiom and designed to map to certain portions of the standard functionality.
•	Configure and 'Configuration' shall mean the setup of the applications using the standard functionality provided within the Axiom Cloud Application release planned for go live.
•	Playback-1: Iteratively design the Axiom Fusion Application after the familiarization session.
•	Playback-2: Solution configured based on signed solution design along with Technical Objects covering integrations and reports with sample data migration.
•	Solution Design Document: the document that captures the solution design (including To-Be process flows) for each line of business.
•	System Integration Test 1 (SIT1): the stage where business processes and 3rd party system integrations with Axiom Fusion Cloud will be tested, led by Axiom Consulting.
•	System Integration Test 2 (SIT2): the stage where business processes and 3rd party system integrations will be tested, led by You and supported by Axiom Consulting.
•	User Acceptance Test or UAT: the stage where business processes in scope will be tested by You as per the agreed UAT test scripts and test plan — this is defined as a Critical Milestone.
•	Cutover: Migration of signed off UAT configurations, signed off UAT technical objects and production data to production environment.
•	Key Personnel: The key members of the implementation team — Program Director, Technical Director, Enterprise Architect, Project Manager, Solution Architect, Technical Architect, Functional Leads and Data Migration Leads.

1.A.2. Implementation Approach
Axiom Consulting and You have agreed upon a phased approach to implement the Project Horizon solution across all SmartAir Group Legal Entities. The implementation approach will proceed in 3 main phases, supported by a global design workstream.

Phase	Definition	Approach
Global Design Workstream	The global design overlaps with Phase 1. Focus is to design and document strategies and enterprise structures for future phases.	Global Design Phase runs from start to finish as specified in Appendix A.
Phase 1: Immediate Priorities for SkyServe	Address SkyServe entities as agreed in scope: Catering, Airport Operations, and Travel lines of business. Leverage and refine the already-implemented Fusion solution for Pioneer Catering.	Implementation in 2 deployments — Drop 1 and Drop 1A. Post-production support as specified in section 1.A.4.10.
Phase 2: Line of business template rollout to Remaining SkyServe Entities	Deploy the templates and strategies developed in Phase 1 for all remaining SkyServe legal entities.	4-drop approach for Phase 2 entities.
Phase 3: Implementation for SmartAir (SA) and SkyServe HQ	Solution for SmartAir HQ, outstations, Hotels, Travel entities, SkyServe Headquarters.	Single go-live. Up to 3 months of Global Design alignment and update for Phase 3.

